#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119585 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119771 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cca9b7c-358a-5f62-9a53-a696df0dd0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Describing a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "fe3edf12-af5b-5bb0-b5b3-efb6cd809134" :question/math-academy-id "e-4394" :question/problem "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n![](images/fc/fc2ed708d717844ca73b7ecbfd8467923fad091ae524153350e7e2fb3df1ea4e.png)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n![](images/52/5260137f2dbf20b44400659be8467da333ff228e5bff323465f920a9505ee5f2.png)\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: $a_{21}=6 \\neq 0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119586 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119772 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b55b50a0-034f-57c0-8a61-883cfb0412dc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "d7c263d4-5d0a-52cd-b876-cfa3bd3171e0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4395" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are lower triangular matrices?\n\n![](images/ad/ad9636de9b8c93338350a6b99d88476b481ed1bf03a5dd64935abedbdb626524.png)" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is a lower triangular matrix since all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrices $A$ and $C$ are *not* lower triangular matrices since they each have a non-zero element above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23} & =1\\ne 0 \\\\ {c}_{13} & =1\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119598 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119784 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e69a4aee-6e92-598b-99b5-1d830b6dea54" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "205d32a2-ac26-5eaf-896a-c6182a70eff7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4498" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n![](images/4d/4dd9b1c1b3d789c166ecd8f6d2a909609c7f4324705c84115cce84a29181bf32.png)\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is upper triangular\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular\n\n- $A^T-A$ is lower triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n![](images/c1/c1ec838cd30cca8fbb2e3996d5a7d84dadb233e1951d05b532a9d606d887eb2f.png)\n\n- Statement II is true, since all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros:\n![](images/f3/f39c68a9b1f5e16caffbf159b629a958e147e14099334b049bdfcd857eef84d2.png)\n\n- Statement III is false, since the result of $A^T-A$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n![](images/f4/f4415c87201f5b92f23e3320c313cd58ac4e720135928645896f976614c5eaa0.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262602 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119771 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cca9b7c-358a-5f62-9a53-a696df0dd0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Describing a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55cec33d-a6da-5626-bbe2-b061760728e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Diagonal matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260607} {:answer/id #uuid "770ef76c-f319-50d7-8a97-d5c775bdeaac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Lower triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260915} {:answer/id #uuid "95a106ed-81ef-5c16-bdbc-d6be56d66200" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Identity matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261173} {:answer/id #uuid "a423decc-250a-5fd2-8836-863cae41272b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Upper triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261305} {:answer/id #uuid "a6349c37-feda-52d9-ab32-111b948babda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Other" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "770ef76c-f319-50d7-8a97-d5c775bdeaac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Lower triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260915} :answer-field/id #uuid "0596aab0-50de-5954-8cdb-1a2aeeaca5a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2b95456b-3323-5d6f-9e68-2195aad3e714" :question/math-academy-id "q-126340" :question/problem "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $C$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: ${c}_{21}=-5\\ne 0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262605 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119772 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b55b50a0-034f-57c0-8a61-883cfb0412dc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37c4a7a7-6201-5e3d-b83c-54214a0f73f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260369} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc900a1-3450-5e9d-9935-fbf3414db9ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260670} {:answer/id #uuid "89212b5f-4485-5c4a-b4e2-c1ef65585d7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261068} {:answer/id #uuid "bebca5d9-6d1a-5817-b8da-7eabbdef4d81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261559} {:answer/id #uuid "ffcb6a99-0bd4-51ca-8095-57e4548dde55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "E=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37c4a7a7-6201-5e3d-b83c-54214a0f73f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260369} :answer-field/id #uuid "58d1ccae-7378-52fd-94ac-13da15be20dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e2e910d3-5a56-5ffe-990b-2c75157e1876" :question/math-academy-id "q-126352" :question/problem "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $D$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $B$, $C$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,E=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120120 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119771 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cca9b7c-358a-5f62-9a53-a696df0dd0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Describing a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76cc8a4b-832c-56c2-8cf5-70501cfbad40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Other" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396033} {:answer/id #uuid "9b6f508a-4794-5f61-a64e-b20147d225cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Identity matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396034} {:answer/id #uuid "82b889e9-c745-5d62-97b1-40fc31c6e4bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Lower triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396035} {:answer/id #uuid "a128b52e-7259-5003-b476-9857977d9aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Diagonal matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396036} {:answer/id #uuid "530ba56a-9b9f-5e98-981e-3ca0aa7acb9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Upper triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82b889e9-c745-5d62-97b1-40fc31c6e4bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Lower triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396035} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc095a3a-82a7-5c30-b624-4fd7e0ceae34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396032}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d6f9badf-44cd-56b4-946a-abae3220a5b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-13759" :question/problem "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: ${a}_{21}=3\\ne 0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269143 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119772 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b55b50a0-034f-57c0-8a61-883cfb0412dc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28741486-369e-5706-ae1b-b725c51b2ab6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266505} {:answer/id #uuid "4e31dd9f-15de-59d3-94cd-966926a7e530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266840} {:answer/id #uuid "533fb3ba-63f1-555e-98ed-8058779ed29c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266889} {:answer/id #uuid "b9bdd702-b2df-5c6c-a4c2-63341c07bd3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267810} {:answer/id #uuid "eadc47d2-6d03-54da-ac2e-565204378e46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e31dd9f-15de-59d3-94cd-966926a7e530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266840} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbef8b98-e8a0-5930-88b8-fc4e670ab6d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268740}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f081148-4183-50c8-903b-3014f5de1d45" :question/math-academy-id "q-13760" :question/problem "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $B$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269148 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119771 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cca9b7c-358a-5f62-9a53-a696df0dd0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Describing a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fb812af-4792-5005-bf12-c4f311aa7f5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Identity matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266422} {:answer/id #uuid "39133468-8ed3-59ca-8b82-06709d2e55a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592